#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Kipi images gallery plugin is a tool for exporting a set of Albums or "
"images to a &HTML; page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: imagesgallery.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: imagesgallery.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kipi"
msgstr "Kipi"

#. Tag: title
#: imagesgallery.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Images Gallery"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This powerful plugin can export your Albums into a &HTML; compliant web "
"image gallery. You can easily select the Albums to export in an &HTML; page "
"and set many designs and parameters for the &HTML; rendering. UTF-8 encoding "
"is used for the best internationalization."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: imagesgallery.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can see some samples built with this plugin at this &URL;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: imagesgallery.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "Collections Selection Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Launching the plugin from within &digikam; displays three tabs to change the "
"settings. The <guilabel>My Albums</guilabel> tab allows you to select all "
"Albums you want to export to &HTML;. Just check the respective Albums (they "
"are displayed without hierarchical nesting). On the next two tabs "
"<guilabel>My Tags</guilabel> and <guilabel>My Searches</guilabel> you can "
"refine your selection using tags or previous search results in &digikam;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: imagesgallery.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Collections Selection Dialog in &digikam;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this plugin &eg; in <application>Gwenview</application> shows another "
"selection dialog with two choices for the content of the gallery, either all "
"pictures in the folder or the pictures you selected before starting this "
"module:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: imagesgallery.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Collections Selection Dialog from other applications"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "Next step is to select a theme for the gallery from this dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: imagesgallery.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Theme Selection Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on the chosen theme you may have additional options to fine-tune "
"the appearance of the gallery."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next screenshot shows the theme parameter setting for the "
"<guilabel>Classic</guilabel> theme:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: imagesgallery.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Parameters for Classic Theme"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For all selected themes you can adjust the settings for the images and "
"thumbnails in the gallery:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: imagesgallery.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Image Settings and Thumbnails Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Full Image</guilabel> section you can either save modified "
"images or <guilabel>Use original image</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For modified images you can select as output format JPEG (smallest filesize, "
"but lossy) and PNG (lossless and free license) and set specific image "
"compression features. If disk space is of concern check the target image "
"compression and lower the compression level from the host application "
"default value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Checking the <guilabel>Max. size</guilabel> box you can fix the maximum "
"target image size (in pixels) with the spinbox at the right. Images bigger "
"than this value will be scaled down to it, but smaller images will not be "
"modified."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If JPEG file format is selected for target resizing images, all EXIF "
"information will be preserved from the original JPEG files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Thumbnails</guilabel> section allows to set the "
"<guilabel>Format</guilabel>, <guilabel>Quality</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Size</guilabel> for the thumbnails in the gallery."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: imagesgallery.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Output Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page defines the settings of where and how to store the gallery with "
"all its associated images. Select a folder or add a new folder with write "
"access where you want the gallery to be written to. Two sub-folders with the "
"name of your album folder and the theme name will be created containing "
"everything."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: imagesgallery.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A progress dialog giving a feedback indicate to user. Press "
"<guilabel>Cancel</guilabel> button during this stage if you want abort the "
"process."
msgstr ""
